ore":8,"flags":0,"comment_count":7,"description":"\u003cp\u003eOutis fights spam generating and sends a fake \"user unknown\" bounce for an email you received, so the sender believes your address does not exist. This isn't a new idea: I created a similar program back in 1998–1999, but I decided to revive it because it should work well with the recent trend of automated emails generated by AI, where the sender might expect a reply; it helps remove your email address from their list.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAny idea on how to improve it? :)\u003c/p\u003e\n","description_plain":"Outis fights spam generating and sends a fake \"user unknown\" bounce for an email you received, so the sender believes your address does not exist. This isn't a new idea: I created a similar program back in 1998–1999, but I decided to revive it because it should work well with the recent trend of automated emails generated by AI, where the sender might expect a reply; it helps remove your email address from their list.\r\n\r\nAny idea on how to improve it? :)","submitter_user":"daniele","user_is_author":true,"tags":["email","privacy","show"],"short_id_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/1h7qzj","comments_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/1h7qzj/outis_fight_ai_spam_by_generating_sending"},{"short_id":"3r00ol","created_at":"2026-10-01T10:04:57.265-05:00","title":"How we built an async-aware Python profiler","url":"https://www.datadoghq.com/blog/engineering/async-python-profiler/","score":3,"flags":0,"comment_count":0,"description":"","description_plain":"","submitter_user":"eatonphil","user_is_author":false,"tags":["python"],"short_id_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/3r00ol","comments_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/3r00ol/how_we_built_async_aware_python_profiler"},{"short_id":"ajtnc6","created_at":"2026-10-01T09:12:03.343-05:00","title":"The Second Golden Spike: Memory Safety Across the Valen/Rust Boundary","url":"https://verdagon.dev/blog/boundary-memory-safety","score":9,"flags":1,"comment_count":0,"description":"","de